<h2>TWIA, flood, and CRS in Aransas County</h2>
<p>Aransas County is in the TWIA designated catastrophe area, and many Rockport owners carry three policies: a homeowners policy that excludes wind and hail, a TWIA windstorm policy, and a flood policy. TWIA covers wind and hail only. Properties in V, VE, or V1-30 flood zones that were built, altered, remodeled, or enlarged on or after September 1, 2009 must show proof of NFIP flood coverage, when available, to get TWIA coverage.</p>
<p>On the flood side, the City of Rockport participates in the NFIP Community Rating System at Class 8, according to FEMA Community Status Book data (April 2025), while Aransas County's unincorporated areas are NFIP participants but not in the CRS. NFIP coverage generally begins 30 days after purchase. See our <a href="/services/flood-damage-claims/">flood damage claims</a> page and the article on <a href="/wind-vs-storm-surge-damage-claims-texas-coast/">wind vs. storm surge damage claims</a>.</p>
<p>TWIA claims must generally be filed within one year of the date of loss, and TWIA has its own timelines for decisions, appraisal demands, and disputes. Our <a href="/services/twia-windstorm-claims/">TWIA claim help</a> page explains them, and the <a href="/claim-deadline-calculator/">claim deadline calculator</a> can help you track dates.</p>

<h2>Repairs, windstorm certificates, and permits</h2>
<p>Re-roofs and roof repairs in the catastrophe area fall under the TDI Windstorm Inspection Program, and TWIA eligibility depends on a certificate of compliance for work done on or after January 1, 1988. Since April 1, 2026, TDI requires windstorm certificate applications to be certified to the 2024 IRC or 2024 IBC. If a contractor skips the windstorm inspection, renewing or keeping TWIA coverage can become a problem. For City of Rockport or Aransas County permit rules, check with the local building office before work starts. The article on <a href="/windstorm-certificate-wpi-8-insurance-claims/">WPI-8 windstorm certificates</a> explains how certificates connect to claims.</p>

<h2>How we help in Rockport</h2>
<p>We document the full loss, including roof coverings, decking, siding, windows, porches, piers where covered, fences, and interior water damage, and we prepare an itemized estimate for your insurer or TWIA. Many Rockport claims involve <a href="/named-storm-hurricane-deductibles-texas/">named-storm or windstorm deductibles</a>, so check yours with our <a href="/hurricane-deductible-calculator/">hurricane deductible calculator</a>. Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement. Start with a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a>, and Corpus Christi Public Adjuster will tell you how we can help.</p>
